From 5fb2bbfa7ce2e0bb3d159243c42f86a852c83d37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:06:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/13] Round 10: Write result JSON directly with static keys

Encode the result envelope, records and domain metrics with static key
bytes instead of the derived serializers. Numbers, strings, IDs,
details and failure values still go through serde_json::to_writer, so
escaping and number formatting are unchanged; the derived Serialize
impls remain for the CLI path and as the reference in a unit test that
asserts byte equality for full, lean, failing and escaped-ID batches.

Workload: serial (96 full records, one worker), full API both sides.
Official 11-sample run: 0.443 ms -> 0.407 ms, 1.09x (paired 1.15x).
41-sample confirmation: 0.425 ms -> 0.361 ms, paired 1.17x.
A first round-10 attempt (pressure tables carried with each saturation
pair) was rejected: its 41-sample paired median was 1.006x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
